{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcvGmKKs9p3YcZ1xESDQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0136rfx8NN4xBoL2ua1tLrQW","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"status":"done","summary":"I added command support for JMAK, over TCP and over SMS. The new class `org.traccar.protocol.JmakProtocolEncoder(Protocol, boolean textChannel)` builds TCP commands as `$<id>;<value>;|...#` and SMS commands as `JMAK#<s|e>;<id>;<value>#...#`. Over SMS, reboot is the literal `JMAK#REBOOT#`. `JmakProtocol` now lists the same 12 command types for data and for text commands. It sets the SMS encoder with `setTextCommandEncoder`, and the TCP pipeline now has a `StringEncoder` plus the encoder. The new `JmakProtocolEncoderTest` checks every command on both channels, including the examples from the task. `make check-fast` passes: Checkstyle is clean and 613 tests ran with 0 failures. I did not run `make check` (the full Gradle build). In the task text, the TCP prefix was garbled, so I used `$`, which is what the examples show. There is no \"movement\" command type in Traccar, so the movement alarm uses `Command.TYPE_ALARM_VIBRATION`.","changes":[{"path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/JmakProtocolEncoder.java","summary":"New encoder: one parameter builder for both TCP and SMS formats. Covers custom, engine stop/resume, output control (index 1/2/3 -> 34/94/167), periodic positions (2), set odometer (30), set connection (13 for an IPv4 server, 43 for a domain, then 12), reboot (93=1 over TCP, JMAK#REBOOT# over SMS), set speed limit (e16=1 then s17), low battery (e57), power removal (e55) and movement (e59)."},{"path":"src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/JmakProtocol.java","summary":"Lists the supported data and text commands, sets the SMS text command encoder, and adds StringEncoder and JmakProtocolEncoder to the TCP pipeline."},{"path":"src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/JmakProtocolEncoderTest.java","summary":"New tes